# Context routing

Read `~/.cursor/my-cursor-setup-catalog.yaml` when choosing skills or personas.

Load only what the current task needs. Do not attach every skill, agent, or rule.

In-session domain personas (do not spawn Task subagents for this):
- React/Next UI → persona `web-ts` (skill `vercel-react-best-practices`)
- Node/Express API → persona `backend-node` (skill `node-api-conventions`)
- Python/FastAPI → persona `backend-python` (skill `python-api-conventions`)
- Terraform/OpenTofu → persona `infra` (skill `terraform-skill`)
- Feature or bug work test-first → skill `tdd` (core; listed on implementation personas)
- Dockerfile / Compose → skill `docker-conventions` (persona `infra`)
- Kubernetes manifests, Helm charts, Kustomize, EKS → skill `kubernetes-skill` (persona `infra`)
- GitHub Actions / `.github/workflows` / `.github/actions` → persona `ci` (skill `github-actions`)
- Superpowers is not part of this repository. Do not assume those plugin skills are present.
- Prisma (schema.prisma, prisma migrate) → persona `db-prisma` (skills `prisma-cli`, `prisma-client-api`, `prisma-database-setup`)
- Python SQLAlchemy/Alembic → persona `db-python` (skill `python-db-conventions`)
- Review of domain code → persona `domain-reviewer` (skill `domain-reviewer`, then the matching domain skill)
- Quality/style, lint, format, or typecheck → rule `quality-style`, then the matching domain skill for tool names

After choosing a persona, load only the skills listed on that persona in `~/.cursor/my-cursor-setup-catalog.yaml` (domain skill(s) plus `tdd` / `verification-before-completion` when listed). Implement and review in this session. Do not spawn Cursor agents from this setup (none are installed). Do not reply with a routing tree instead of doing the work.

`.ts` is not enough to choose web-ts vs backend-node. Use the user's task and paths.

Prisma vs SQLAlchemy from the user's task and paths; `.ts`/`.py` is not enough.

Terraform, Docker, and Kubernetes/Helm are persona `infra`. Pick the skill from the task and paths; `*.yaml` is not enough.

GitHub Actions is persona `ci`. Pick it from the task and paths (`.github/workflows`, `.github/actions`); `*.yml` is not enough to choose `ci` vs `infra`.

Production env files (`.env.production`, `.env.prod`, `.env.production.local`, `.env.prod.local`): do not read them. Do not ask the user to paste their contents into chat. Tell the user to apply or edit those files themselves.

If catalog.yaml and an agent's or persona's skill list disagree, the catalog wins.
